        "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1559788694709473280/j1s3zm5m_normal.jpg",
        "verified": true
      },
      "created_at": "2026-11-16T10:24:43.000Z",
      "text": "A video showing Tamil Nadu Social Justice Minister Vanni Arasu allegedly pursuing a tiger inside the Mudumalai Tiger Reserve has sparked controversy, with conservationists demanding action against him. The video shows the minister and his family travelling in Forest Department safari vehicles, getting out of vehicles, moving closer to wildlife and trekking inside the reserve. He is also seen sitting on a car bonnet and posing for pictures with forest staff and officials.\n\nThe BJP has criticised the minister, alleging violations of forest rules that prohibit visitors from dismounting, chasing or approaching animals inside the reserve. BJP leader Narayanan Thirupathy called for a transparent inquiry, saying, \"Conservation laws cannot be compromised for those in power.\" Conservationists have also urged the Forest Department to register a case against the minister under the Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972, for allegedly disturbing wildlife.\n\n#TamilNadu #VanniArasu #Tiger #MudumalaiTigerReserve #BJP",
      "lang": "en",
      "public_metrics": {
